<title>GERMANY: MAN truck unit sees lower 1996/97 sales.</title>
<headline>MAN truck unit sees lower 1996/97 sales.</headline>
<dateline>MUNICH, Germany 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>MAN Nutzfahrzeuge, the truck making unit of MAN AG, said on Thursdaay that it expected 1996/97 sales to fall six percent and output to decline 10 percent.</p>
<p>The company also said it expected a &quot;clear decline&quot; in earnings during the year, chairman Rudolf Rupprecht told a news conference.</p>
<p>In the 1995/96 business year which ended June 30, the unit reported a 10 percent increase in sales to eight billion marks and an increase in pre-tax profit of 24 percent to 50 million marks.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
